  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: FilicÄƒu (Romanian partnership trick-taker). Setup: 4 players in 2 fixed partnerships (opposite seats). 32-card German deck (Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells). 8 cards dealt per player. Trump set by bottom card flipped by dealer (if Over-Knave, keep flipping). Gameplay: 8 tricks. Lead player (right of dealer) starts, proceeds anticlockwise. Follow suit if able; must trump if void; must play trump if no suit. Scoring: 1 point for each Ace, 1 for each Ten (8 total). Master status: partnership with 5+ points. Slave status: losing partnership (4-4 split special).',
    Player: "Welcome to FilicÄƒu, a Romanian trick-taking partnership game. You and your opposite partner compete against the other pair. Play 8 tricks using a 32-card German deck. Capture Aces and Tens (1 point each). Watch out for the Over-Knavesâ€”they're the highest trumps! The partnership with the most points becomes the Masters.",
    objective: 'Collect as many Aces and Tens as possible. There are 8 total points (4 Aces, 4 Tens).',
    gameplay: "1. Lead: Player to dealer's right leads.\n2. Follow Suit: You must follow suit if possible.\n3. Mandatory Trumping: If you cannot follow suit, you MUST play a trump if you have one. If you have neither the suit nor trumps, you may discard any card.\n4. Over-Knaves: These always belong to the trump suit, regardless of their printed suit logo.",
    keyRules: [
      'No Passing: You cannot hold back a trump if you are void in the led suit.',
      'Anticlockwise: All play and dealing moves to the right.',
      'Winning condition: Collect as many Aces and Tens as possible.',
    ],
